            <ArticleTitle>An unusual case of congenital short trachea with very long bronchi mimicking bronchial asthma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>372-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Case reports of a short trachea with early branching of the main bronchi are uncommon. The case is presented of a 64 year old woman with upper airway obstruction due to this anatomical abnormality which caused breathlessness and wheezing that was misdiagnosed (and treated) as bronchial asthma for many years.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
